+`list --summary` prints counts instead of job rows, for dashboards and agents that
+only need totals. It performs the same scan, supervisor observation and history
+collection as `list`, and renews, signals and rewrites nothing. Each job counts in
+one category:
+
+- `active`: `starting`, `running` or `stopping`.
+- `unverified`: `unknown`, or a finished state without a recorded finish time.
+- `finished`: every other job.
+
+`selected` counts the jobs the same `list` would show (the default recent window,
+or every retained job with `--all`). `retained` counts every readable job record in
+the state directory, with or without `--all`. Each `total` is the sum of its three
+categories. Human output is two lines on stdout, plus the usual `Warning:` lines on
+stderr:
+
+```text
+selected: 4 (active 1, unverified 2, finished 1)
+retained: 9 (active 1, unverified 2, finished 6)
+```
+
+`list --summary --json` prints one object with `schema_version: 1`, `selected` and
+`retained` (each with integer `total`, `active`, `unverified` and `finished`) and
+the same `warnings` as `list`; there is no `jobs` key. Apart from warnings, summary
+output holds no per-job data (IDs, argv, cwd, labels, URLs, errors), and its size
+does not grow with the number of jobs. Unreadable records are reported as warnings,
+not counted. As with `list`, warnings do not change the exit status.
+`--summary` combines with `--all` but not with `--resources`; `watch` has no
+summary mode.
+
 ## Install the skill
 
 The same [skill folder](https://github.com/jaredchu/proclease/blob/v0.1.6/skills/proclease/SKILL.md) works as an instruction-only
